KZ3 patch 2204: S7.0 measurement probes (RSX_O0=1, RSX_O0_S7=1): [s7-fill] split of the FILL bucket, [s7-bar] barriers and the overlap bound, [s7-draw] eligibility/bytes/device cache, [s7-page] page census and the resident-page break-even, [s7-ww] write-watch microprobe (RSX_O0_S7_WW=1). Probe only, default off, no behaviour change.

Review fixes: ld_s7_draw runs inside its own split bucket (RSX_SB_X_S7, folded into `other`, printed as s7draw_ms in [s7-fill]); the hash unit cost is measured on a cold 32 MiB buffer in a stride order, not a hot 4 KiB page; clocks is bumped atomically; an unmet acquire is counted once per acquire (re-polls of the same FIFO position are not); the page sampler is a multiply-shift (unbiased for any RSX_O0_S7_PAGE_SAMP).

